# Background removal is locked (commit `9059edd`)

This lock applies **only** to the artwork background-cut algorithm in `services/image_processing.py`.

It does **not** lock logo sizing, overlay fit, name/number placement, transfer widths, cart, checkout, or admin production measurements. Those may be changed freely.

Kayleigh confirmed this cut is perfect. Do not "improve" it, add GAME DAY special cases, or bring rembg back unless she explicitly asks to change the algorithm.

## What it does

In `services/image_processing.py`:

1. Sample the paper color from the image border
2. Delete **only that color**, everywhere it appears (letter holes included)
3. Keep every pixel that is a **different** color (lavender, parchment, gold, navy)
4. Peel 1–2px of blended fringe on the new edge
5. Crop

Tight tolerance (`~16–36`). No rembg. No border-only flood. No "preserve enclosed cream."

## Do not

- Raise the color tolerance (that ate parchment and gold text)
- Run rembg on uploads (OOM / timeouts)
- Restore enclosed background-colored regions
- Add GAME DAY / distressed-field exception paths

Uploads stay fast because this is numpy-only. Client timeout is 45s.
